\section{Columns}{
One of the main objectives of \code{tidyDCM} is to abstract the complexity of
working with several different libraries. Thus, it always returns the same
columns:
\itemize{
\item \strong{number} Integer. Number of the item used as identifier.
\item \strong{item} Character. Name of the item used as identifier extracted from the
Q-matrix.
\item \strong{rule} Character. Condensation rule used to convert the item parameters
to correct response probabilities (e.g. GDINA, DINA, RDINA). See "Rules,
link functions and DCM models" section for more information.
\item \strong{link_fun} Character. Link function (e.g. logit, identity)
\item \strong{term} Character. The attributes required for this parameter to be
considered (e.g. the term "1-3" is included for masters of both attribute
1 and 3). See "Terms and Logic Gates" section.
\item \strong{order} Integer. How many attributes are included in the term. Intercepts
are 0, main effects 1, two-way effects 2, and so on.
\item \strong{estimate} Double. The parameter itself.
\item \strong{SE} Double. If it was estimated, this is also included.
}
